{"name":"Hypodermic needle gauge dimensions (OD, ID, wall thickness, dead volume)","description":"The physical dimensions behind a needle gauge number: nominal outer diameter, inner diameter, wall thickness, and dead volume per 25.4 mm of needle. Gauge number alone is not enough to answer 'will this needle prime my 10 uL syringe' or 'what is the ID of a 26s needle' — the wall marker ('s', 'RW') changes the ID at the same gauge, and dead volume is what actually determines whether a small-volume syringe can be primed. Two independent publishers are cited and they agree where they overlap: Hamilton, a syringe maker, covers 34 gauge down to 10 gauge with dead volumes; New England Small Tube, a tube manufacturer, covers 6 to 27 gauge in regular wall with millimetre figures of its own. Each keeps its own naming, so the same needle can appear twice — as '18 gauge needle' and as '18 RW' — with a separate quote behind each.","url":"https://referencesource.org/syringe-needle-gauge-dimensions/","licence":"Dimensional facts (a physical tolerance table) are not copyrightable; cited with attribution to the publishing vendor's technical reference page. No page content beyond the per-gauge figures is reproduced.","last_verified":"2026-08-27","stale_after":"2029-08-26","sources":["https://www.hamiltoncompany.com/laboratory-products/needles-knowledge/needle-gauge-chart","https://nesmalltube.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Metric_Chart_Web.pdf"],"records":[{"gauge_number":"6 RW","outer_diameter_mm":"5.15","inner_diameter_mm":"4.39","wall_thickness_mm":".381","id":"6-rw","url":"https://referencesource.org/syringe-needle-gauge-dimensions/6-rw/","source":"https://nesmalltube.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Metric_Chart_Web.pdf","source_quote":"6      RW   5.15   5.13/5.18   .381   4.39     4.32/4.47","verified_fields":["gauge_number","inner_diameter_mm","outer_diameter_mm","wall_thickness_mm"]},{"gauge_number":"7 RW","outer_diameter_mm":"4.57","inner_diameter_mm":"3.81","wall_thickness_mm"